  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 114 PM CDT Mon Jun 29 2026\n\nThe potent upper level ridge continues to lock into place over the \nregion today. Highs expected in the mid 90s with dew points in the \nupper 70s. This will lead to heat indices generally in the 105+ \nrange. The ridge is expected to stay in place through late week, \npossibly into the weekend. An Extreme Heat Warning is in effect as \nheat indices remain in the 105+ range through Friday and possibly \ninto Saturday. \n\nBy Thursday the ridge axis shifts more east and begins to \npotentially relax a bit. This introduces the chance for some \nisolated to scattered (20-30%) showers and storms over portions of \nthe area during the afternoon and evening. Chances continue into the \nweekend as the ridge breaks down. PoPs pick up to around 30-40% \nSunday afternoon as a shortwave moves through mainly to our\nnorth.",
